components=['Proved a uniform norm bound for the discrepancy between an actual finite complex mean and an actual probability integral, including empty algebraic samples without claiming they are probability measures.', 'Extended the ORIGINAL bounded cube alpha law to EVERY fixed continuous test on the actual compact cube quotient. A fixed Lipschitz approximation and the genuine Haar probability bound preserve endpoint, residue and fixed-modulus uniformity. Derived the actual standard alpha-window local law for continuous tests.', 'Proved that length-first local approximation and actual empirical comparison at each FIXED alpha force equality of the limiting integrals. No diagonal alpha(m), illicit exchange of limits, or uniform Lipschitz assumption on projection/face maps is used.', 'Proved actual empirical comparison for all fixed Lipschitz tests extends to all continuous tests on a compact metric space. Combined this with the local-limit comparison and measure extensionality to obtain actual projected measure invariance for a continuous map.', 'Applied the transfer to the genuine nativeResidueCubeHaarImage and the ORIGINAL polynomial cube orbit with exact standard windows and period residues. The actual projected empirical-comparison premise is explicitly retained; supplying it from selected alignment arrays remains unfinished. This theorem alone is NOT a proof of marginal face invariance.']
remaining='StrongConjecture remains UNPROVED; goal ACTIVE; no unavoidable obstruction established. Common-witness original point/cube local laws, continuous cube alpha-window tests, actual global point-mixture weak limits, projected Haar full support and measure-to-setwise support transfer are proved. The genuine original-cube empirical-comparison-to-projected-Haar-invariance implication is now proved, conditional on the ACTUAL empirical comparison. Remaining: exact identification of countably selected native alignment array evaluations with the required projected original full-cube orbit and derivation of their fixed-alpha comparison limits, then projected face measure/set invariance; genuine marginal-to-joint lifts and weighted-shear recurrence/full Alignment; separate arbitrary-input GTZ interval Gowers LINEAR nilsequence inverse; final positive distinct rapidly separated SAME-color ALL nonempty FS AND FP. No source/Haar/character/inverse oracle or new axiom introduced. Author checks are not independent kernel replay or external peer review. Keep the user-requested GitHub repository PRIVATE. Public repository/PR/prize milestone not reached.'
review='Author mathematical review, 2026-10-14.\nPinned OpenAI sections 7 (original cube local limits) and 8 (face invariance).\n\nThe finite discrepancy operator is explicitly the finite normalized sum minus\nan ACTUAL integral against a probability measure. Its norm bound is 2 times the\ncontinuous-test sup norm. An empty finite sample has algebraic mean zero; it\nis never called an empirical probability measure. Linearity uses integrability\nof continuous functions on the compact probability space.\n\nFor each continuous cube test f, choose ONE Lipschitz g within epsilon/6.\nApply the proved ORIGINAL bounded alpha law to g with its actual finite sup\nnorm and Lipschitz constant and tolerance epsilon/3. The discrepancy operator\nbounds the replacement error by 2*epsilon/6. The resulting scale is uniform\nover the original allowed endpoints/residues/moduli, for this fixed test.\nIt is not a claim of uniform approximation over ALL continuous tests. Actual\nHaar probability and metric-compatible quotient Borel structures are used.\nThe standard-window corollary instantiates the existing exact geometry with\nc=C=1, base residue b and zero increment residues. L tends to infinity so\npositive real lengths hold eventually. No source replacement takes place.\n\nThe numerical comparison lemma fixes epsilon and chooses a SINGLE positive\nalpha below both local radii. Only then is the sequence index sent large\nenough for the two local estimates and their actual empirical difference.\nThe triangle inequality forces equality of the limiting integrals. This is\nlength-first and never assumes convergence for a diagonal alpha(m).\n\nTo extend an empirical comparison to continuous tests, approximate a fixed\ncontinuous test once by a Lipschitz test, bound the error of each finite mean\nby epsilon/4, and use the eventual epsilon/4 comparison for that same fixed\nLipschitz test. Empty sets cause no issue for the algebraic bound.\n\nFor projected measure invariance, pi and T are only continuous. Do not claim\neither is globally Lipschitz. The preceding extension first supplies comparison\nfor EVERY continuous target test. Pullbacks F o T o pi and F o pi are continuous\non the source; its actual local law and the ordered-limit lemma equate their\nintegrals. Real bounded continuous tests are embedded into complex tests, and\nactual pushforward integral identities plus finite-measure extensionality give\nT_*(pi_*mu)=pi_*mu. All probability/finite-measure hypotheses are discharged.\n\nThe final native theorem supplies this local law from the genuine ORIGINAL\nstandard-window theorem and sets mu to nativeResidueCubeHaarImage with the\nliteral same filtration, period, rational residue and smooth curve. It retains\nthe exact empirical comparison as a premise. The common original-source\nfactorization theorem from the preceding round supplies the bounded local law;\nno independent curve or source is selected here.\n\nLIMIT: the actual selected native-array states are not yet identified with\nthis projected original full-cube orbit. That equality and the resulting\nfixed-alpha comparison limits must be proved; they must NOT be replaced by an\nunproved source oracle or assumed global Lipschitzness. Thus actual marginal\nface invariance remains unproved. The prior full-support bridge is available\nonly AFTER the genuine measure-invariance premise has been discharged.\nJoint lifts, recurrence/full Alignment, arbitrary-input GTZ inverse and the\nfinal same-color FS/FP theorem remain unfinished. No full-target claim.\nAuthor audit is not independent kernel replay or peer review. Keep PRIVATE.\n'
